<title>UK: William Cook buys back shares at 248p.</title>
<headline>William Cook buys back shares at 248p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British steel company William Cook Plc said on Monday that it had bought back just under 1.1 million shares at 248p per share during the day.</p>
<p>The purchase was made pursuant to a general authority given at the company's annual meeting on August 2, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>The company's shares had earlier closed up 9.0 pence at 242.5p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
